<<~ ahu #/head>>

! openNodeVessel ~ one preparation, two doors

Node supplies the platform atoms — filesystem storage, the relay and its auth gate, a worker pool —
and the capability pieces it alone holds. Everything above that comes from the shared keel.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/law>>

!! The invariants

# ''ONE preparation, run by BOTH doors.'' The atoms, the keel and the boot closures build once, and
the two entry points differ ONLY in which capability stack they compose over that single preparation.
A second preparation per door would let the doors drift while both still opened.
# ''A HEARTH lifts what a FACE carries.'' The base course plus the caps a lit face brings.
# ''A CROSSROADS serves an HTTP floor.'' The base course plus the caps that floor needs — no wiki, no
pool. The daemon stays, because the immune core rides in every vessel, and bag registration omits the
user-wiki bags where no wiki stands.
# ''Each stack DECLARES itself at its compose site.'' The composition derives from that declaration
rather than from a table one layer up, so a reader finds the answer where the choice happened.
# ''The node vessel holds NO semantic privilege.'' It carries roads, docks and sync. Live VM state
lives in sovereign islands — the daemon and the wiki — and a host that also held meaning would make
every other vessel a client of this one.
# ''All Node-specific code lives HERE.'' The trim tab: a platform detail anywhere else spreads a
second Node into code that claims isomorphism.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/edges>>

